Pattern matching is useful when one value can take several meaningful shapes.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    if score is {
        case < 0: io.line("invalid")
        case 0: io.line("zero")
        case >= 90: io.line("excellent")
        else: io.line("other")
    }
]

Each pattern arm starts a logical line with `case`. A colon ends its header. Moth evaluates the subject once and runs the first arm whose pattern matches and whose guard, if present, is true.

Use `else:` for everything that was not matched earlier. It can have an empty
body when the remaining cases should do nothing.
